.TH MCR-EDIT 1 "August 2026" "rusty-midnight-commander" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcr-edit \- internal editor started as mcr \-\-edit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcr
.BR \-e " | " \-\-edit
[\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B mcr
.BI \-\-edit= FILE
[\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens rusty-midnight-commander’s internal editor (the
.B mcedit
equivalent) instead of the dual-pane listing.
.PP
With no files, one empty untitled buffer is created. Each given path
is opened as a separate editor screen (Screen list switches among
them). This page is original Apache-2.0 text covering the shipped
editor CLI and keys. It is not a copy of GNU
.BR mcedit (1).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B F2
Save.
.TP
.B F4
Replace.
.TP
.B F7
Search.
.TP
.B F9
Editor menu (File / Edit / Search / Command / Options).
.TP
.B F10
Quit (confirm if the buffer is dirty). Esc Esc also quits.
.TP
.B F12
Save as (Shift-F2 on terminals that send F12).
.TP
.B Alt-l
Go to line.
.TP
.B |
Pipe the selected block through an external command.
.TP
.B Ctrl-r / Ctrl-a
Record / replay a macro.
.PP
Insert vs overwrite, autoindent, tab width, and syntax highlighting
are editor options. F4 from a directory panel edits the highlighted
file without using this CLI.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcr (1),
.BR mcr-view (1),
.BR mcr-diff (1)
